# catingiran (`cti`) v1.0.0 — Full User & Configuration Guide

**catingiran** (`cti`) is a fast terminal IDE and code editor written in pure C11 under the **BSD-3-Clause** license with zero third-party build dependencies. It combines Vim modal grammar, an asynchronous JSON-RPC 2.0 LSP client, VS Code-style file explorer sidebar, buffer tabs, split panes, code runner, and a built-in plugin manager.

---

## 1. Build, Install & Uninstall

```sh
git clone https://github.com/netanyahy/catingiran.git
cd catingiran
make
sudo make install   # or: doas make install
```

After installation:
* `cti` and `catingiran` are installed to `/usr/local/bin`.
* Default preset config is copied to `/usr/local/etc/catingiran.conf` and `~/.config/catingiran/catingiran.conf`.
* Plugins reside in `~/.config/catingiran/plugins/`.

To uninstall:
```sh
sudo make uninstall
```

---

## 2. Configuration (`~/.config/catingiran/catingiran.conf`)

Open your config directly inside the editor with **`:conf`**, and apply edits without restarting using **`:reload`**.

### Appearance & Themes

| Option | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `theme` | `charcoal` | Color theme: `charcoal`, `obsidian`, `catppuccin`, `tokyonight`, `nord`, `light` |
| `show_tabs` | `true` | Show top bufferline tabs |
| `statusline` | `true` | Show bottom mode/file/Git statusline |
| `line_numbers` | `true` | Show gutter line numbers |
| `relative_numbers` | `false` | Hybrid relative line numbers around cursor |
| `cursorline` | `true` | Highlight active cursor line |
| `colorcolumn` | `100` | Vertical ruler column (`0` disables) |
| `nerd_icons` | `true` | Nerd Font file/folder icons (`false` for plain ASCII/Unicode) |

### Indentation & Editing

| Option | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `tab_size` | `4` | Tab width (`1`–`16`) |
| `expand_tab` | `true` | Insert spaces instead of `\t` |
| `auto_indent` | `true` | Auto-indent new lines |
| `auto_pairs` | `true` | Auto-close `()`, `[]`, `{}`, `""`, `''` |
| `highlight_current_word` | `true` | Highlight matching occurrences of word under cursor |
| `trailing_whitespace` | `true` | Highlight trailing spaces/tabs on lines |
| `trim_on_save` | `false` | Strip trailing whitespace on `:w` |

### Scrolling, Input & Search

| Option | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `scrolloff` | `0` | Context lines to keep above/below cursor (`0`–`20`) |
| `mouse` | `true` | Mouse clicks (tabs, sidebar, editor) & scroll wheel |
| `russian_keymap` | `false` | Map Cyrillic keys in Normal/Command mode (`ж`->`:`, `р/о/л/д`->`h/j/k/l`) |
| `ignore_case` | `true` | Case-insensitive `/` find and `:%s` replace |
| `smart_case` | `true` | Case-sensitive if query contains uppercase letters |
| `hl_search` | `true` | Highlight all search matches on screen |

### History, Panels, LSP & Plugins

| Option | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `undo_levels` | `500` | Maximum undo/redo history depth (`u` / `Ctrl+R`) |
| `confirm_quit` | `true` | Prevent `:q` when buffers have unsaved changes (use `:q!`) |
| `sidebar_open` | `true` | Open file explorer on startup |
| `sidebar_width` | `28` | Sidebar width (`16`–`60`) |
| `sidebar_side` | `left` | Sidebar position: `left` or `right` |
| `show_hidden` | `false` | Show dotfiles in sidebar (`H` toggles live) |
| `output_height` | `8` | Output drawer height (`4`–`30`) |
| `auto_complete` | `true` | Show live completion popup while typing |
| `autocomplete_min_chars` | `2` | Minimum prefix chars before auto-popup (`1`–`10`) |
| `auto_lint` | `false` | Run linter automatically on save |
| `lsp_enabled` | `true` | Enable async LSP client (`clangd`, `pyright-langserver`, `jdtls`) |
| `lsp_auto_hover` | `false` | Reserved option for auto-hover behavior |
| `git_branch` | `true` | Show Git branch in statusline |
| `plugin` | `python`, `c`, `java` | Enable official pack or `user/repo` GitHub plugin |

---

## 3. Asynchronous LSP Support

When opening C/C++, Python, or Java files, `cti` automatically launches matching LSP servers in `$PATH` over non-blocking JSON-RPC pipes:
* **C / C++**: `clangd`
* **Python**: `pyright-langserver --stdio` (fallback: `pylsp`)
* **Java**: `jdtls`

LSP features:
* Real-time diagnostics (`●` error / `▲` warning in gutter, full message in bottom bar when cursor is on line).
* `gd` — Go to Definition (`textDocument/definition`).
* `gr` — Find References (`textDocument/references`).
* `K` — Floating Hover documentation card (`textDocument/hover`, `Esc` dismisses).
* `Space + r n` — Rename symbol across workspace (`textDocument/rename`).
* `:lsp` — Show active LSP servers, PIDs, and status.
* Live LSP completion items integrated into the Insert mode popup (`Ctrl+Space` or automatic).

---

## 4. Built-in Plugin Manager (`catingiran Plug`)

* `:PlugList` — browse official packs (`python`, `c`, `java`, `web`, `git-extras`).
* `:PlugAdd <name|user/repo>` — append plugin to `catingiran.conf` and install immediately.
* `:PlugCreate <name>` — scaffold a custom plugin in `~/.config/catingiran/plugins/`.
* `:PlugStatus` / `:PlugInstall` / `:PlugUpdate` / `:PlugClean` — manage installed plugins.

---

## 5. Vim Counts, Text Objects, Macros & Search/Replace

* **Counts**: `5dd`, `10j`, `3k`, `3w`, `4x`, `3p`, `5u`, `5Ctrl+R`, `15G`, `15gg`.
* **Text Objects (`c`/`d`/`y` + `i`/`a` + obj)**: `ciw`, `diw`, `yiw`, `di"`, `da"`, `di'`, `da'`, `di(`, `da(`, `di{`, `da{`, `di[`, `da[`, plus Visual `vi(`, `vi{`, `vi"`, `viw`.
* **Macros**: `qa` starts recording into register `a` (`[REC @a]`), `q` in Normal stops recording, `@a` / `3@a` / `@@` replays.
* **Substitute**: `:%s/old/new/g` (whole file) and `:s/old/new/g` (current line).
* **Undo / Redo**: `u` and `Ctrl+R` (or `:redo`).

---

## 6. Commands & Shortcuts (`<Space>` = Leader)

* `:w [file]`, `:q`, `:q!`, `:wq`, `:x`, `:e file`, `:new`, `:bd`, `:bn`, `:bp`, `:t1`..`:t9`
* `:ot`, `:ht`, `:tree` / `Ctrl + B` / `F2` / `Space + e` — file explorer (`H` hidden, `a` create, `r` rename, `d` delete).
* `:vsplit`, `:split`, `:only` / `Ctrl + W` / `Space + v/s/x` — split panes.
* `:run` / `F5` / `Space + rr` — build & run current file; `Ctrl + J` (`:out`/`:ho`) — output drawer.
* `:find` / `Ctrl + P` / `Space + ff` — fuzzy file finder; `:grep text` / `Space + fg` — project grep (`Enter`/`gf` jump).
* `:git`, `:diff`, `:stats`, `:term`, `:lint`, `:fmt`, `:ft <lang>`, `:theme <name>`, `:set <opt>`.
* `gcc` / `gc` (Visual) — toggle line comments; `J` / `K` (Visual) — move lines; `m` / `M` — bookmarks; `]d` / `[d` — next/prev diagnostic.
